==Trivia==
*Restricted Area's Japanese name, Yuragi no Kinsei Kuiki (ゆらぎの禁制区域, "Forbidden Zone of Fluctuation"), may refer to [[wikipedia:Quantum fluctuation|quantum fluctuations]] and [[wikipedia:Band gap|band gaps]], also known as forbidden gaps or forbidden energy gaps.
*Some of the stages' names reference real scientists and sciences:
**[[Fleming Seaway]] could refer to [[wikipedia:John Ambrose Fleming|John Ambrose Fleming]] or [[wikipedia:Alexander Fleming|Alexander Fleming]]. The word フレミング ''Furemingu'' (Fleming) in its Japanese name can also be taken as "Flemming", as in [[wikipedia:Walther Flemming|Walther Flemming]].
**[[Euler Archipelago]] references Swiss mathematician, physicist, astronomer, geographer and engineer [[wikipedia:Leonhard Euler|Leonhard Euler]]. It may specifically be a reference to [[wikipedia:Euler's laws of motion|Euler's laws of motion]] that was lost in translation, as 運動 ''undō'' (motion) sounds similar to 群島 ''guntō'' (archipelago).
**[[Heaven-Defying Fruit]]'s Japanese name, Ten'i ni Somuku Rakka (天意に背く落果, "Fallen Fruit That Disobeys Heaven's Will"), may be a reference to the falling apple that inspired [[wikipedia:Isaac Newton|Isaac Newton]]'s gravitational theory.
***Heaven-Defying Fruit may also reference the [[wikipedia:Fall of man|fall of mankind]] in Abrahamic religions, in which Adam and Eve ate the forbidden fruit of the tree of knowledge, disobeyed God, and fell from the Garden of Eden. This works with the sub-chapter's Japanese name, which can be translated as Forbidden Zone of Fluctuation.
***[[Dogenstein]] is the only enemy in Heaven-Defying Fruit who is not described as a comedian in Japanese. His presence there along with the "Heaven-Defying" in the stage's name and ゆらぎ ''Yuragi'' (Fluctuation) in Restricted Area's Japanese name may reference [[wikipedia:Albert Einstein|Albert Einstein]]'s quote criticizing quantum fluctuations, "[[wikipedia:Hidden-variable theory#"God does not play dice"|God does not play dice]]".

